From 6e418d2a29fffe73735ed45514533c9a24a7bb36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObliviOS Build <build@localhost>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:31:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] oblivios: let Settings choose and remove the Duress Unlock
 finger

A finger chooser behind the Duress Unlock screen: it lists the enrolled
fingers, asks for the second PIN or password and links the chosen finger.
The main screen gains Choose and Remove entries, and changing the second
credential links the finger again. DuressUnlockFingerFlow holds the rules
without Android types and is tested on the JVM. Strings are in
strings_oblivios.xml.

Not compiled: Settings has no host-side type-check here.
